# Generated from the OSRS Wiki page "Transcript:Jungle Potion" by tools/quests/transcript_to_dialogue.py
0	section	Starting off
1	line	Trufitus	Greetings Bwana! I am Trufitus Shakaya of the Tai Bwo Wannai village.
1	line	Trufitus	Welcome to our humble village.
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	What does Bwana mean?
2	line	Player	What does Bwana mean?
2	line	Trufitus	It means friend, and friends come in peace. I assume that you come in peace?
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	Yes, of course I do.
3	line	Player	Yes, of course I do.
3	line	Trufitus	Well, that is good news, as I may have a proposition for you.
3	select	Select an Option
3	option	A proposition eh? Sounds interesting!
4	line	Player	A proposition eh? Sounds interesting!
4	line	Trufitus	I hoped you would think so. My people are afraid to stay in the village.
4	line	Trufitus	They have returned to the jungle and I need to commune with the gods
4	line	Trufitus	to see what fate befalls us. You can help me by collecting some herbs that I need.
4	select	Select an Option
4	option	Me? How can I help?
5	line	Player	Me? How can I help?
5	line	Trufitus	I need to make a special brew! A potion that helps me to commune with the gods. For this potion, I need very special herbs, that are only found in the deep jungle.
5	line	Trufitus	I can only guide you so far as the herbs are not easy to find. With some luck, you will find each herb in turn and bring to me. I will give you details of where to find the next herb.
5	line	Trufitus	In return for this great favour I will give you training in Herblore.
5	select	Start the Jungle Potion quest?
5	option	Yes.
6	line	Player	It sounds like just the challenge for me. And it would make a nice break from killing things!
6	line	Trufitus	That is excellent Bwana! The first herb that you need to gather is called
6	line	Trufitus	Snake Weed.
6	line	Trufitus	It grows near the vines in an area to the south west where
6	line	Trufitus	the ground turns soft and the water kisses your feet.
6	action	end
5	option	No.
6	line	Player	Hmmm, sounds difficult, I don't know if I am ready for the challenge.
6	line	Trufitus	Very well then Bwana, maybe you will return to me invigorated and ready to take up the challenge one day?
6	action	end
4	option	I am very sorry, but I don't have time for that.
5	line	Player	I am very sorry, but I don't have any time for that.
5	line	Trufitus	Very well then, may your journeys bring you much joy.
5	line	Trufitus	Maybe you will pass this way again and you then take up my proposal?
5	line	Trufitus	But for now, fare thee well.
5	action	end
